/-!
# Genuine restriction compatibility of original period-family classes

Exact restriction of the original sheaves and genuine integer endpoints
give actual native Ext pullbacks. Original free-open representing maps
identify them with the native cohomology-presheaf restriction. Literal
holomorphic pullback and the original restriction biholomorphisms then
give the true neighborhood comparison for nested original base opens.

The actual period-cocycle classes commute with that restriction for
arbitrary holomorphic coefficients defined only on the larger open.
In particular, the two original holomorphic coefficient functions give
a genuine additive presheaf morphism into the original pushed-forward
degree-one cohomology presheaf. No local frame, generation, or
higher-direct-image isomorphism is asserted by this package.
-/
